     5	## §0 — Cycle shape (WAVE form — throughput correction, HQ 2026-11-14)
     6	- Trigger: cron `study-recreation` or HQ charge. **A cycle is a WAVE, not an item:** up to **5 owed items** per cycle (starting price), taken in recreation-queue order, each carried to a scored verdict.
     7	- **Fan-out:** each item's build + Codex wave is an independent agent task — the cycle spawns one subagent per item with the item's full §1–§5 charge; the seat coordinates, verifies each item's filings firsthand (scores.md arithmetic, purity of the filed build), and closes the cycle record. T15's attempt is the measured unit: one bounded build + four Codex runs, not a 6-hour job.
     8	- Run directory `runs/<date>-cycle-<NNN>-wave-<K>/` opens BEFORE any building; its RUN.md holds the wave manifest (items, per-item parameter tables + verification plans summarized, links to per-item records) — each item ALSO gets its working record inside its artifact directory (`build-record.md`). Building first and writing the spec after is the inversion and does not ship.
     9	- Artifact directory per item: `hidden_files/study/recreations/<technique-id>-<slug>/` — created at Plan, holds segment cut + recreation.html + comparison.html + scores.md + codex/ returns.
    10	- **Batch re-pricing:** the first waves measure real per-item cost (wall time, failure modes); the wave size is re-priced from that evidence at Condense and reported to HQ — 5 is a starting price, not a law.
    11	- **Cadence derivation (printed, not just scheduled):** while OWED + IN-PROGRESS items outnumber the RECREATED pool, waves fire every **3 h** — at wave 5 that is up to 40 first attempts/day against a 22-item backlog (≈0.6 days nominal to clear, before digestion adds more). As the catalogue approaches mostly-RECREATED, cadence relaxes toward maintenance — the relaxation is a printed judgment with its reason, filed as an amendment + reported, never a silent schedule drift.
    12	- **Empty-pool form (promoted 2026-11-15, Cycle 010 Condense — candidate filed in Cycle 009's Condense; promotion condition was a second empty firing demonstrating the same shape, and Wave 8 is that firing; clause wording derives from the Cycle-009 candidate):** a wave with zero owed first-attempt items is a lawful cycle, not a skipped one. Its product is the finding form: (1) a pool census priced from the QUEUE recreation section, the catalogue register (TECHNIQUES.md + INDEX.md), the intake directory, and a binding artifact census (per-directory scores.md + codex/ return presence), plus board hand-offs where intake is pending; (2) the cycle-level guard firings — codex-observe in its cycle-level form, jev-observe-exit, jev-plan-exit, codex-condense — fired unconditionally, with per-item/per-build calls (codex-plan-review · jev-prewave · the five-lens scoring wave) printed NOT-DEMANDED-BY-FORM with their reasons; (3) the filings (HQ.json entry · verdict-history no-verdict line · lane heartbeat beat); (4) upstream intake state priced in the open (what is built, what stands unregistered/unadopted, which job owns the next act) — an empty pool here is never printed as an empty lane upstream, and the next wave's Observe re-censuses fresh rather than inheriting the finding. No item is invented, no practice re-attempt is misrouted, and no verdict is counterfeited for an unbuilt wave. First demonstration: Cycle 009 Wave 7 (2026-11-14). Second demonstration + this promotion: Cycle 010 Wave 8 (2026-11-15).
    13	- **Completion-wave form (Amendment A8, 2026-11-16, Cycle 021 Condense — re-encoded under codex-condense REVISE before landing):** a wave whose predecessor stopped mid-Execute/Verify is completed by the next cycle: the completing cycle's §1 prices each unfinished item's on-disk state (artifact census + which prescribed calls already fired), and before any standing payload is fired its hash binding to the filed build is verified. Completion items occupy wave slots and count toward the §0 cap; new items fill only the remaining slots. The completing cycle restates per item the standing guidance dispositions and mechanics citations the item's Plan binds to (a prior cycle's §2b is evidence, not working memory), and carries each mid-attempt item to its verdict on the filed builds: hash-bound payloads and filed gate returns are consumed, never silently re-fired or rebuilt; where an item's record layer is missing (no build-record, no A6 legs, no gate filings), the completing cycle authors it from cited sources — the filed build plus the predecessor cycle's §§1b/2/2b — with the sources printed on the authored record's face and no fact claimed from builder memory, then fires the missing prescribed calls. First demonstration: Cycle 021 Wave 18 (2026-11-16) — T123 payloads consumed · T124 prewave consumed · T129 record authored from filed build + Cycle-020 §§1b/2/2b · T130 taken in the remaining slot.
    14	- **Skeleton record at Plan close (adopted 2026-11-16, Cycle 021 Condense — practice Amendment A-C015-1's candidate form, charged to this job on its HQ board as rec-2026-11-16-skeleton-disposition; NON-SKIPPABLE):** before Execute opens, the wave writes (a) its HQ.json board entry skeleton — cycle id, the wave's items, state "planned — Execute not yet run" — and (b) its lane heartbeat skeleton beat in the same state. The cycle's close then UPDATES those skeleton entries in place (same ids) with the outcome; it never creates the record at close. A cycle whose board/heartbeat record was first created at its close prints deviation **D-SKELETON** in its RUN.md. (Evidence: recreation Cycle 017 + Cycle 020 and practice Cycles 013 + 015 — cycles that completed Observe + Plan, died before close, and left no board/heartbeat trace; Cycle 020's five built artifacts stood unreported until Cycle 021's census found them. Cycle 021 itself prints D-SKELETON: the charge stood on the board before this cycle opened and its Observe missed it — the adoption lands here, first demonstration is the next cycle.)
