    16	## §1 — Observe (what good Observe means for THIS job)
    17	1. Read the technique's catalogue entry (packet digest.md section + TECHNIQUES.md entry): mechanics, timestamps, why-it-works, evidence frames. View the evidence frames firsthand — the recreation is built from the technique's mechanics, and a mechanic the builder has not seen is a guess.
    18	2. Read the original segment in motion: the archived source at the catalogue timestamps (the cut is made in §3, but Observe watches the segment in the source first and notes the sub-beats: what forms when, holds how long, dissolves how).
    19	3. Extract the technique's VARIABLES: every property that could change without changing the technique (text content, phrase count, timing/durations, palette, scale, direction, density). A variable not named in Observe becomes a hardcoded accident in Execute.
    20	4. Name the consumer: which production surface will lift this machinery (container type + the lane that owns it).
    21	Gate out: mechanics summary + sub-beat timings + variable list + consumer, in RUN.md.
    22	- **RESOURCE LIST (read in this order, every wave):** (1) `../QUEUE.md` recreation-queue section — current positions, OWED status, ownership split (first attempts here; scored techniques route to practice) · (2) the item's packet section in its digest.md + TECHNIQUES.md entry (style-library) · (3) the item's prior scores.md + codex/ returns + `verdict-history.md` lines, including named family siblings (e.g. T16 reads T15's filings) · (4) the evidence frames + archived source segment in motion · (5) this file's Amendments A1/A3/A5 guidance for the item's family (flow-field model + Owner Cures 1–2 for particle fields; runtime text sampling for typography) · (6) `guards/guards.md` command list.
    23	- **Codex call point (Observe):** `guards/codex-observe.md` fires per item at §1 step 1 (source-record audit) on every cycle. Its receipts persist in RUN.md's Observe section; a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.
    24	- **Observe-exit call:** `guards/jev-observe-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the gate-out block per item before §2 opens for that item. The phase advances on the verdict's recorded disposition (applied, or set aside with reason; applied gaps are carried into §2 as named charges). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
    25	
    26	## §2 — Plan
    27	1. **Parameter table:** config object design — every §1.3 variable becomes a named config key with the specimen's value as its default. The recreation reads ALL of its content/timing/palette from config; literals inside the animation logic are a Plan failure.
    28	2. **Construction choice:** the HTML-native construction that fits (canvas particle system, CSS keyframes, SVG draw-on, DOM animation, generated imagery + overlays) — chosen for the technique's mechanics, with the rejected alternatives named in one line each.
    29	3. **Bar pricing (standing, priced at founding 2026-11-13):** consolidation requires Codex wave average ≥85 AND no lens under 70. Priced judgment: the average alone would let a fatal lens (purity at 40) hide inside three good scores; the per-lens floor is what makes the bar a proof rather than a vibe, and 85 is high enough that a PASS means production can lift the machinery without re-deriving it. The bar stands as charged unless a scored cycle produces evidence against it — then the evidence goes to HQ, the bar does not move silently.
    30	4. **Verification plan:** swap test design (which config values change — at minimum the words; plus one timing and one palette value), purity checks (§6.1 greps + asset inventory), comparison sync method, and the Codex wave composition (four lenses, §5).
    31	Gate out: parameter table + construction choice + verification plan, in RUN.md.
    32	- **Plan's standing product:** the Execute checklist (§3 steps as an itemized list) AND the Verify checklist (each deliverable property with its checking instrument — swap-test altered values, purity grep patterns, comparison check, jev-prewave call point, five-lens wave composition) AND the failure-point evaluation (per item, priced from this job's record: convergent freeze · intensity collapse · phrase overlap · fitting limits · render-proof limitation), all in RUN.md at this gate.
    33	- **Plan-exit call:** `guards/jev-plan-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the Plan product per item (parameter table · checklists · failure points · plateau priced in Plan per Amendment A2 — prior/family average + the stuck-lens hypothesis stated before Execute, not discovered at close) before §3 opens. `guards/codex-plan-review.md` fires alongside it for every item. Both verdicts are advisory: the phase advances on their recorded dispositions (applied, or set aside with reason). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
    34	
    35	## §3 — Execute
    36	1. **Cut the original segment** from the archived source at the catalogue timestamps (±0.5 s handles) into the artifact directory as `segment.mp4`, re-encoded for browser playback. The segment is EVIDENCE: it appears in the comparison labeled ORIGINAL, and nowhere else. Bulk media stays local (sync pointer rule).
    37	2. **Build `recreation.html`** — one self-contained HTML file (the fleet's form): config object at the top, construction below it, no external assets except generated imagery the build itself creates and files beside it. No captions/subtitles anywhere in the build (fleet law) — text that IS the technique (e.g. the words being formed) is the subject, not a caption.
    38	3. **Build `comparison.html`** — the deliverable's face: original segment and live recreation side by side at matched size, ONE synchronized control set (play/pause/restart drives both; the recreation's clock slaved to the video's currentTime or to a shared start timestamp), each side labeled (ORIGINAL — <specimen> @ <timestamps> · RECREATION — <technique>, parameterized). On a phone-width screen the two stack vertically with the controls still reachable (fleet tappability law).
    39	4. **Self-verify before Codex** (§5 legs 1–3); a build that fails its own swap test does not spend a Codex wave. Self-verify files the A12 executable receipts (§5 leg 3b) in the build-record's first draft; a build-record missing receipts does not spend the prewave call either.
    40	Gate out: segment + recreation + comparison on disk; self-verify recorded.
    41	- Execute follows the Plan's Execute checklist and fires the Verify guards named in the Plan's Verify checklist — no step is improvised past the checklist; a step the checklist cannot cover returns the item to §2 (REVISE), it is not invented in Execute.
    42	
    43	## §4 — (reserved; keep numbering stable for trace rows)
    44	
    45	## §5 — Verify (the Codex scoring wave + own checks)
    46	1. **Swap test (own, mechanical):** load the recreation with altered config (different words, one changed timing, one changed palette value) — by URL parameter or config edit in a scratch copy. The technique must still read correctly. Record the exact altered values + the result. A break = FAIL, return to Execute; Codex is not fired on a build that fails its own swap test.
    47	2. **Construction purity (own, mechanical):** grep the recreation for the original's media (segment filename, source filename, frame-sequence patterns, <video>/<img> pointing at specimen media) — any hit is a refusal-class defect (§6.1). Asset inventory: every asset the recreation loads is listed and is either code or generated/created by this build.
    48	3. **Comparison check (own):** both sides play from the shared control; durations matched to the segment; labels correct; phone-width stacking holds.
    49	3b. **Pre-wave Jev gate:** `guards/jev-prewave.md` judges the build record after legs 1–3 and before the wave (leg 4): FIRE-WAVE spends the wave; HOLD returns the build to Execute with its classification and the wave moves to its next item. **Receipt readiness check (Amendment A12, 2026-11-18 — performed by the builder BEFORE the payload is assembled):** every A11 checkpoint in the build-record carries its executable receipt — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A checkpoint with a claim but no receipt returns the record to the builder before the call is spent. **Receipt-index reconciliation (Amendment A13, 2026-11-18):** the build-record carries a RECEIPT INDEX enumerating (a) every guards.md command applicable to the item and (b) every A11 assertion for the item; before the payload is assembled the builder reconciles the index against the applicable guard commands, the item's planned A11 assertions, and — for a completion or re-attempt — the assertion sets established in the filed prior harnesses and their amendments, and, for census receipts, against the build's expected CONFIG keys (nested/array keys included). Every index line carries its executable receipt or an explicit NOT-DEMANDED line whose disposition cites the governing plan or guard; a missing expected line, an unsupported exclusion, or a line with neither returns the record to the builder. A receipt is valid only if it carries the evidence its assertion requires: for each CONFIG-derived input, the CONFIG expression and its evaluated value; for each check, the raw observed result. A populated receipt lacking that evidence returns the record to the builder on the same form. This check is a readiness check for the mandatory call, not a gate on it: the call still fires at its step on every cycle, and a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE under the standing firing ruling. The deliverable-class judgment for this job IS the five-lens scoring wave (leg 4, defined in `guards/codex-scoring-wave.md`) — no separate jev-verify file exists, by design: the wave's per-lens verdicts + leg 5's mechanical consolidation are the deliverable gate, and a second Jev over the same deliverable would duplicate them.
    50	4. **Codex scoring wave (external):** FIVE reviewers, distinct lenses — **motion fidelity · timing/tempo match · construction purity · reusability/parameterization · readability** (the fifth lens is permanent since 2026-11-14, Amendment A5: formed-word legibility against the particle field — word-vs-reserve intensity separation present and sufficient · the word readable at phone size during its hold · background particles never competing at word intensity). Each run: instruction file opens with the standing header (consumer + the decision the run prices; the working record it builds from and writes to; the return must name what it wrote into the body), carries the technique's catalogue mechanics + the recreation's full source, and returns ONE lens score (0–100) + priced findings. Feeding follows the fleet's Codex rule (instructions + artifact in ONE stream; never pipe + stdin field together). Returns are filed verbatim under the artifact's `codex/` directory.
    51	5. **Consolidation verdict (mechanical):** average of the five lens scores ≥85 AND minimum lens ≥70 → PASS. Else FAIL. The arithmetic is shown in scores.md; no rounding up across the bar.
    52	Gate out: scores.md complete (four lens scores + returns pointers + verdict + arithmetic); tier hand-off filed to style-library (its board) with the verdict; TECHNIQUES/INDEX tier moves are style-library's act.
    53	
    54	## §6 — Guards (standing, every cycle)
    55	1. **Construction purity (refusal-class):** the recreation is HTML/CSS/JS + generated/created assets only. Embedding the original video, a frame sequence of it, or a traced redraw of a frame as the "recreation" is a refusal-class defect — the cycle stops, the defect is recorded, the build is discarded. The original appears ONLY as the labeled comparison side.
    56	2. **Parameterized, not traced:** content, timing, and palette come from config. The swap test is the enforcement; a recreation that only works with the specimen's exact words is a copy, whatever its code looks like.
    57	3. **Scoring integrity:** four lenses, four separate runs, returns filed verbatim before the verdict is computed; a missing lens = no verdict (the wave is incomplete, printed as such). Scores from a prior attempt never carry into a new attempt's average.
    58	4. **Tier honesty:** until scores.md shows PASS, the technique is IN PROGRESS (attempt filed) or DESCRIBED (no attempt) — the catalogue prints the tier the evidence supports, and this job's reports use the same words.
    59	5. **No captions/subtitles** in recreation or comparison (fleet law); technique text is subject, not caption.
    60	6. **Production-law boundary:** a RECREATED tier proves the technique is replicable in HTML. It does not by itself clear the technique for a shipping short — production's own laws (asset construction, placement, ear) govern adoption. The catalogue entry states this boundary where a technique's construction would collide with a production law (e.g. particle construction vs the production cutout law — the recreation proves the *effect*; production decides its lawful construction).
    61	
    62	## §7 — Faithfulness trace (adopted 2026-11-13 from the template draft)
    63	Every RUN.md closes with the draft's fields, as fields not prose: trace table (one row per §; missing = UNACCOUNTED), choice log (≥2 alternatives; SINGLE-PATH printed), deviation register (draft §0 enums; empty prints EMPTY-BY-CHECK + checks), evidence binding (path + size/sha/line/re-probe; UNVERIFIED at the claim), git corroboration (UNCORROBORATED-BY-LOCAL-GIT until JOB-14's sync extension lands lane files and is verified — lane board lane-2026-11-13-003), size discipline (§8).
    64	
    65	## §8 — Size discipline
    66	Norm (wave form): up to 5 items per cycle, one artifact directory each, fanned out in parallel. A technique whose build balloons (a whole scene instead of the technique) splits WITHIN its item: the item's Plan product is the split — core mechanic first, ornament as a later attempt on the same directory. An item that cannot reach a scored verdict inside its wave files its state honestly (IN PROGRESS with what stands) — a wave never holds its other items hostage to one stuck build.
    67	
    68	## Amendment A1 (2026-11-13, from Cycle-002 — T15 attempt 1)
    69	1. **Convergent-lens rule (§5 reading rule):** when two or more lenses independently name the same defect, that defect is priced as the next attempt's primary cure, ahead of single-lens findings. (T15 attempt 1: motion 68 + reuse 64 both named the surplus-particle freeze during FORM.)
    70	2. **Typography construction precedent:** runtime sampling of config-rendered text is the lawful letterform construction (purity 100, T15 attempt 1) — future typography recreations start from it rather than re-deriving purity.
    71	
    72	## Amendment A2 (2026-11-13, the funnel design — score-delta floor rule, HQ's priced addition)
    73	**Re-attempt floor rule:** a re-attempt whose average does NOT beat the technique's prior attempt average is not filed as silent progress — its scores.md entry carries a WHY section naming the plateau (what was changed, what did not move, which lens is stuck and the hypothesized cause). Grinding the same score without a named plateau is the ceremony pattern in miniature and is a deviation (PLATEAU-UNNAMED) in the attempt's RUN. Score deltas are reported in the library's growth accounting (style-library GROWTH.md) per attempt, not only at consolidation.
    74	
    75	## Amendment A3 (2026-11-13, owner's refinement to the recreation law — UNIVERSAL obligation)
    76	1. **The queue orders; it never exempts.** If a catalogued lesson is a motion graphic that can be recreated as HTML, its recreation MUST be created. Triage survives only as ordering + pacing. Classification rule, applied per technique at registration and printed in the open: (a) is it a motion graphic (its lesson is motion/animation behavior, not a still, a system, or a story structure)? (b) can HTML/CSS/JS + generated assets carry that motion? Yes+yes = **OWED**. A no on either leg is priced with its reason in QUEUE.md and the tier register (T24 static end card: no motion content — documentation asset; T25 two-world system: a design system whose component techniques are individually owed — not itself one recreation).
    77	2. **Tier accounting consequence:** a motion-graphic technique at DESCRIBED prints as **OWED + its queue position** (style-library Amendment A3 enforces the face).
    78	3. **Division of labor with the practice job:** this job owns FIRST attempts (unattempted techniques, queue order). Re-attempts of already-scored recreations belong to the practice job (lowest-scored first). A technique mid-attempt here finishes its verdict here before practice can pick it up.
    79	
    80	## Amendment A5 (2026-11-14, the owner's own read on T15 attempt 1 — two cures + the fifth lens)
    81	The owner heard the four Codex returns verbatim, converged with the wave on the frozen-flow defect, and caught TWO defects no lens named. Both are standing law now:
    82	1. **OWNER CURE 1 — foreground/background intensity separation (readability):** particles forming the word render FOREGROUND (contrast/opacity/intensity separated); reserve particles render BACKGROUND (dimmer). Same-intensity fields make formed words unreadable — in the original, the separation is part of why the words read at all. Any particle-field recreation carries this separation by construction.
    83	2. **OWNER CURE 2 — strict phrase sequencing (phase exclusivity):** a phrase's formation may not begin until the previous phrase's dissolve has completed; one word's lifecycle owns the stage at a time. Overlapping lifecycles are a defect class in any sequenced recreation.
    84	3. **THE FIFTH LENS — READABILITY (permanent, §5.4):** the founding evidence is priced: four lenses scored a recreation whose words fight their own background, and none owned legibility. The owner's expectation now has a judge (the golden rule). Attempt 2 onward is scored by five lenses; the bar form is unchanged (average ≥85, no lens <70) with the fifth lens inside both terms. Attempts scored under the four-lens wave keep their filed averages — cross-wave comparisons print the lens count (a 4-lens 78.5 and a 5-lens score are different instruments; deltas across the boundary are labeled as such).
    85	4. **Flow-field construction model (HQ's implementation note, standing guidance for particle techniques):** model the pool as ONE constant flow field, not per-phase animations — every particle always carries the stream's directional velocity; forming = BORROWING particles out of the flow onto targets, where they keep low-amplitude jitter (never zero velocity), with a guaranteed reserve fraction that is never borrowed; dissolving = RELEASING them back to full stream velocity with continuity (no velocity replacement at phase boundaries). The intensity separation rides the borrow flag: borrowed = foreground, reserve = background. This single model carries Owner Cure 1, Owner Cure 2's clean stage handover, and attempt 1's convergent defect (frozen surplus) at once.
    86	
    87	## §9 — Condense
    88	Read the run's traces + Codex returns → candidate lessons (which constructions scored well on which lenses; recurring Codex findings across techniques) → label demonstrated/candidate/planned → promote into this file (dated, technique cited) + verdict-history.md → next cycle inherits. A lens finding that recurs across two techniques is a pattern: it becomes a §6 guard candidate with the two citations.
    89	- **Condense Codex call point:** `guards/codex-condense.md` fires at Condense close — it attacks the cycle's drafted amendments for faithfulness (does the amended text encode the lesson) and four-layer coverage (steps · mechanical guards · Jev definitions · Codex prompts; each untouched layer carries a NO-DEFECT proof or a named not-yet-amended reason). A REVISE returns the named amendment for re-encoding before the cycle record closes. Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE. (Built 2026-11-14.)
    90	
    91	## §10 — Delivery / reporting
    92	- Completion reported on this job's HQ.json + lane heartbeat: technique, attempt #, five lens scores + average, verdict, artifact path.
    93	- Owner-facing presentation routes through HQ. PASS or FAIL, the report carries the scores — a FAIL with its priced gap is a complete cycle; hiding it would be the defect.
    94	
    95	## Judgment-layer presence evaluation (standing — owner's 100% order, 2026-11-14)
    96	Before this job's Condense closes, every cycle, evaluate the judgment layer AS HOSTED IN THIS JOB'S OWN HOME (the `guards/` directory at the home root): (a) every judge this job's deliverables demand is present as its own file there — Jev calls (instruction + call command), deterministic guards, Codex review instructions for the review types this job repeats; (b) each is current against this cycle's experience (a verdict reversed, a defect that passed, a review that missed — each either amended its file in this Condense or is named in the cycle record as not-yet-amended with its reason); (c) any judge the deliverable demanded this cycle that does not exist yet is CREATED in this step or carried as a named build charge with pilot sequencing — never noted-and-dropped. The verdict prints in the cycle record: **JUDGMENT LAYER: COMPLETE** (all demanded judges hosted + current) or **INCOMPLETE** (missing/stale judges named). INCOMPLETE is a lawful print; a silent Condense is not. JOB-05's census reads this field fleet-wide.
    97	Founding print (2026-11-14): JUDGMENT LAYER: **INCOMPLETE** — mechanical guards hosted + demonstrated (5/5); Codex scoring wave defined in-job and demonstrated in four-lens form (five-lens form demonstrates at its first wave); jev-prewave designed, **UNBUILT** — build charge carried in this job's Condense until armed.
    98	
    99	**Ruling addendum (2026-11-14 ~20:55 EST — owner's judgment-call ruling):** arming = firing. This job's Jev/Codex steps are non-skippable and fire unconditionally in its next live cycle, raw responses filed in the run record; verdicts are advisory — applied, or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense + the call-file amendment it teaches. The founding print above reads superseded where it phrases any call as gated, conditional, or UNBUILT-blocked; presence from the next cycle prices whether the prescribed firings HAPPENED (a cycle closing without one is INCOMPLETE).
   100	
   101	## Amendment A6 (2026-11-15 — HQ owed-checks charge: the two legs are BUILT and WIRED)
   102	The measured-fit leg and the config-census leg — candidacy text since Waves 5–6 — are built as standing guards: `guards/guard-measured-fit.md` and `guards/guard-config-census.md` (v3.1 codified, including application-site resolution for nested/array keys and the CSS-variable setter check). **Pre-wave step (non-skippable):** for every item in a wave, after the build and BEFORE the five-lens scoring wave fires, both legs run on the item's final recreation.html and their outputs file in the item's artifact directory (`fit-table.md`, `config-census.md`); the wave RUN cites each leg's path + hit count per item. A wave record lacking either leg's output for any item prints **INCOMPLETE**. Leg verdicts are advisory (owner's 2026-11-14 ruling): hits are cured pre-scoring where the builder can, or carried into the wave printed with their disposition; misses (a leg's false hit or missed defect) are recorded in Condense with the guard-file amendment they teach. Scope: the legs own the fit and config classes only — timing anchors, density judgment, and content failures are NOT theirs and are never presented as cured by them.
   103	
   104	## Amendment A7 (2026-11-15, Cycle 013 Condense — pattern rule fired: T64 + T66 timing lenses)
   105	**Schedule basis is a required Plan field.** The §9 pattern rule fired this cycle: two techniques' timing lenses independently priced the same defect class — a recreation whose schedule is silently re-based from the segment's measured timeline (T64 lens-timing −16: calendar entrances at 0.4/1.4 s vs measured ~4/5 s · T66 lens-timing-interim1 −18: opening state mismatching the measured window). Standing requirement, binding on every Plan from Wave 12 onward: each item's window-scope line in the wave RUN.md names its **schedule basis** — `segment-anchored` (the build's phases sit at their measured segment times), `t=0 allocation` (the technique's lifecycle is re-based to the build's own zero, with the re-basing named as an allocation), or `two-act` (a measured-window act plus a labeled allocation-model act) — and the item's build-record carries the same line. A Plan whose window-scope line lacks the schedule basis is incomplete in the same way a Plan lacking its swap values is (jev-plan-exit prices it). Landed by Cycle 013's Condense under the pattern rule; HQ may amend or retire it, and until then it is operative instruction, not candidacy.
   106	
   107	## Amendment A9 (2026-11-16, Cycle 023 Condense — the five Cycle-022 NOT-YET-AMENDED landings, plus this cycle's pattern promotion)
   108	Landed by Cycle 023's first Replan item, the named consumer of Cycle 022 §9's five outstanding amendments. Each clause is operative instruction, binding from Wave 21 onward.
   109	1. **Plate construction is a Plan requirement (A9.1).** Any Plan adopting a moving background plate prices its construction in the parameter table: for techniques where a moving plate IS the technique (the RSVP family form), the plate is a seamless tiled pan — repeat period = pan wrap, pan clock continuous across cycle wrap, and **tiles endpoint-periodic** (a tile whose end state differs from its start state steps at the join — T139 motion lens, Cycle 023). For a case-only stream technique (T137's form), the Plan prices a still plate — any background motion exceeds the technique.
   110	2. **Gate-order sequencing (A9.2).** No build script is written before the Observe-exit and Plan-exit returns are filed and consumed in the wave's §2b. A draft produced earlier is a deviation printed in §2b, never silently rebuilt over.
   111	3. **Count assertion (A9.3).** Every table-driven build prints source-count vs built-count and halts on mismatch — in the item's build-record (builder side) AND in the wave record's own summary lines (seat side): a summary count in a gate or Verify section is machine-counted against the table it summarizes before that section closes, and a mismatch blocks the section's closure until the record carries the corrected count with its source note. (Founding catches: T134's truncated sentence table, Cycle 022 · the §2b 33-vs-37 summary in Cycle 023, caught builder-side before this landing.)
   112	4. **Raw-output filing (A9.4).** Build-records file the raw harness output (swap test, purity grep, syntax check) from the first draft, not a summary of it; a build-record whose own-checks section carries claims without the raw output beneath them is an ASSERTED-CHECKS defect at jev-prewave.
   113	5. **Gate-out reasoning inline (A9.5).** A gate-out section carries its dispositions' reasoning inline — the construction-precedent dispositions (A1 §2's scope, A5's applicability) are stated with their reasoning in the Observe gate-out itself, not only in a later Plan section the gate judge is not fed. (Founding miss: Cycle 023's jev-observe-exit GUIDANCE-DROPPED return — the reasoning stood in §2 while the judged record was §1.)
   114	6. **Parameterization depth (A9.6 — pattern promotion, §9 rule: the reusability finding recurred across T139 + T140 in Cycle 023, both lens-minimum at 78).** Every subject-shaping value is CONFIG data, not a code literal: vehicle/geometry branch data, background-layer geometry and growth/opacity coefficients (a background layer's coefficients are subject-shaping when a lens can price them against the subject — the T140 dust classification is resolved this way), and plate tile data. The config-census leg (A6) prices literals of these classes as HITs from Wave 21 onward; guard-config-census.md's classification text is amended in the same landing's guard sweep or carries the not-yet-amended note in the cycle record that first applies it.
   115	
   116	## Amendment A10 (2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — the three bundled restatements whose named consumer was this Condense)
   117	Landed by Cycle 026's Condense, discharging the carry recorded in Cycle 025 §9 item 1 and Cycle 026 §0b item 1. Each clause restates at instruction level a form already operative in the guards or gate contracts; each is binding from Wave 23 onward (Wave 23 complied with all three, filed in its run record).
   118	1. **Prewave payload completeness (A10.1 — restates §5 leg 3b at instruction level; operative since Cycle 024 in jev-prewave.md's context contract).** The jev-prewave payload for every item MUST carry that item's A6 leg outputs (fit-table.md + config-census.md) verbatim. A payload lacking either leg's output is a feeder defect printed in the wave's §5; a prewave verdict priced without them does not discharge leg 3b.
   119	2. **Plan census-anchor mapping (A10.2 — restates the Cycle-025 Plan form at instruction level).** Every schedule table in a wave's Plan prints its census-anchor mapping: the window-start offset (segment-anchored or t=0 allocation), the census states in segment-relative ms, and the prescribed state at each instant the table governs. A schedule that departs from its census prints its departure table beside it (the Wave-22 defect class: census printed in §1, schedule derived from other numbers, the gap found only by the timing lens at verdict cost). Plan-exit judges price an absent mapping or departure table as REVISE.
   120	3. **Motion-census Observe form (A10.3 — restates the Cycle-025 Observe form at instruction level).** §1 files a frame census at ≤2 s spacing across each item's transitions (seat-extracted, viewed firsthand by the seat), full SHA-256 per frame, with the motion findings stated per item: which instants carry motion, which are holds, and what changes between census states. Findings priced from a digest's prose alone, without the census, do not close Observe.
   121	
   122	## Amendment A11 (2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense — census-checkpoint assertions; adopting the practice job's census-checkpoint note, practice Cycle 019 Condense, carried as a candidate by Cycle 027 §9.1 and adopted here on three independent demonstrations)
   123	Every item maps each Observe census checkpoint to an executable own-check assertion and its CONFIG-derived evaluation instant. The build-record identifies the checkpoint, the assertion, the CONFIG expression, and the evaluated result. jev-prewave returns ASSERTED-CHECKS if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent. A CONFIG timing swap must move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Demonstrations: practice T153 (timing 45→92) + T162 (timing 64→96), practice Cycle 019 · recreation Wave 25, all four items (timing lenses 92/96/96/100, no timing-stuck item, against Wave 22's allocation-vs-census timing failures at 68/64). Enforcement lives in jev-prewave.md §2 leg (3), amended in the same landing.
   124	
   125	## Amendment A12 (2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense — the ASSERTED-CHECKS pattern: T190 · T192 · T196 · T197 prewave HOLDs in one wave; T195's cure path as the positive demonstration)
   126	1. **Receipt form (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, referenced from §3 step 4).** Every A11 assertion in a build-record files its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT beside the claim — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A9.4 already required raw output; this clause names the receipt's three parts and wires the check into the prewave step itself. A build-record whose assertions carry claims without receipts is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the call's firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, and an unfired call still prints the cycle INCOMPLETE).
   127	2. **Fit evidence form.** In this seat (no browser binary), the lawful fit measurements are (i) harness post-fit ink measurement of the built spans, or (ii) rendered measurement with a named stand-in font — each row printing its instrument, the fitted element + stage geometry, the measured ink bounds, and the margin (guard-measured-fit.md, amended in this same landing: items 1–2 + output form). A character-width × factor MODEL is a HIT under that guard, never a measurement. Demonstrations: T195 (harness post-fit ink measurement → prewave FIRE-WAVE, wave PASS 88.6) · T190 (PIL rendered measurement, named stand-in) · counter-instances T196 + T197 (model rows priced as HITs).
   128	3. **The two-HOLD stop + completion re-fire.** The two-HOLD stop stands unchanged: a second HOLD files NO VERDICT with cures priced, and the wave is not fired on that build. The item's completion — cures filed, fresh own-checks + A6 legs on the cured build, then ONE jev-prewave re-fire, and on FIRE-WAVE the five-lens wave bound to that build — is the next recreation cycle's first charge in completion form (§0 A8). This clause explicitly authorizes that single completion-cycle re-fire so A8's consume-don't-refire rule (which binds gate returns and hash-bound payloads of the ORIGINAL attempt) is not read as barring it: the re-fire judges a cured build that no prior return has seen. The item does not route to practice unscored (A3 §3: a technique mid-attempt here finishes its verdict here).
   129	
   130	## Amendment A13 (2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense — the receipt-completeness pattern: T190 · T196 · T197 · T199 prewave HOLDs in one wave; T192's 1.0-clearance as the positive demonstration; re-encoded under codex-condense REVISE before landing)
   131	1. **Receipt index + reconciliation (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, extended in the same landing).** Every build-record carries a RECEIPT INDEX enumerating (a) every guards.md command applicable to the item (1 purity · 2 swap · 3 syntax + seeded-RNG census · 4 arithmetic, seat-side · 5 segment binding · 6 fit leg · 7 census leg · 8 census-anchor probes where a zero-state anchor stands) and (b) every A11 assertion for the item. Readiness REQUIRES the reconciliation, not just the index: against the applicable guard commands, the item's planned A11 assertions, and — for a completion or re-attempt — the assertion sets established in the filed prior harnesses and their amendments; census receipts reconcile against the build's expected CONFIG keys (nested/array keys included — founding miss: T190's `scenes[].id` row). Every line carries its executable receipt or an explicit NOT-DEMANDED line whose disposition cites the governing plan or guard; a missing expected line, an unsupported exclusion, or a line with neither is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, per A12.1's form).
   132	2. **Assertion inheritance.** A completion/re-attempt builder inherits the prior attempt's assertion set WHOLE (every checkpoint the prior harness evaluated, by name); an assertion leaves the set only by a printed disposition in the new build-record, tied to the governing plan or guard. A re-derived set that silently drops an assertion is a builder defect printed in the record (founding instance: T197 Cycle 036, CP4-`or`).
   133	3. **Receipt validity (evidence form, not presence).** A receipt is valid only if it carries the evidence its assertion requires: for each CONFIG-derived input, the CONFIG expression and its evaluated value (never a bare number whose CONFIG dependence the judge must take on faith — founding instances: T196's boundary-skip endpoints · T199's census twins); for each check, the raw observed result. Item-specific evidence stands under its own assertion (founding instance: T199's joined CP11 receipt stands under CP11, not as an appendix claim). A populated receipt lacking its required evidence returns the record to the builder under §5 leg 3b's readiness check.

