    46	8. **Census-anchor probes (2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 025 Condense — mechanical layer of the allocation/count consistency landing).** Where a census anchor asserts an empty/zero state at a named instant (e.g. "no territory at 449 s"), the builder's own-checks harness MUST probe the recreation's state function at that instant (mapped segment-relative) and file the raw result in build-record.md; a prescribed schedule that is nonzero at a zero-state anchor is a build-record defect to cure BEFORE the wave, not a finding for the timing lens to discover. Forcing evidence: T160 Wave 22 (prescribed purple front 8.33% grown at the 449 s zero-state anchor; timing lens priced it 68 in `hidden_files/study/recreations/T160-expansion-front-envelopment/codex/lens-timing.md`).
     1	# Jev call — jev-observe-exit (recreation)
     2	
     3	_Per-call definition from jev-call-template.md. Built 2026-11-14 (phase-guard augmentation). The judgment: a recreation wave may not enter Plan on a catalogue summary alone — Observe must have priced the queue, read the prior scores where they exist, seen the evidence frames, and carried the standing construction guidance into working memory._
     4	
     5	## 1. What it judges
     6	- Deliverable: the wave's Observe working memory — RUN.md gate-out block (§1: mechanics summary + sub-beat timings + variable list + named consumer) for each item in the wave (up to 5 owed items).
     7	- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §1, at the gate out of Observe, before §2 Plan opens for any item in the wave. The verdict is advisory per item: applied, a RETURN-TO-OBSERVE item is held out of the wave's Plan (the wave proceeds with its advancing items; a held item never holds the wave hostage — same rule as jev-prewave §5); set aside, the miss is recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
     8	
     9	## 2. Instruction (the model's charge)
    10	Judge whether this Observe record can support a Plan for THIS recreation wave, item by item. Price, in order:
    11	(1) QUEUE STATE PRICED — does the record state the recreation queue's current position (../QUEUE.md read this cycle), each item's queue number and OWED status, and the ownership split (Amendment A3 §3: this job owns FIRST attempts; an already-scored technique belongs to practice — a wave item that is a re-attempt is a routing defect, named)? T15 is the standing example: attempt 1 scored FAIL 78.5 on 2026-11-13, so T15 attempt 2 is practice's charge, never this job's wave item.
    12	(2) PRIOR SCORES READ — for any item whose technique already has a scores.md or a verdict-history line (a techniques' family sibling counts: e.g. T16 shares T15's particle machinery), does the record cite the actual filed scores and cure list, or does it plan from the catalogue description alone? Planning that ignores a filed failure is the defect this leg exists to catch.
    13	(3) MECHANICS SEEN, NOT SUMMARIZED — does the record carry the packet section's mechanics + sub-beat timings from firsthand viewing of the evidence frames and the source segment in motion (§1.1–1.2), with timings in seconds — or only a restatement of the TECHNIQUES.md one-liner? A mechanic the builder has not seen is a guess (§1.1).
    14	(4) VARIABLES EXTRACTED — is the §1.3 variable list complete for this technique (text content, phrase count, timing/durations, palette, scale, direction, density — plus technique-specific variables), so Plan's parameter table has something to bind? A variable missing here becomes a hardcoded accident in Execute (§1.3).
    15	(5) CONSTRUCTION GUIDANCE CARRIED — where the technique's family has standing guidance, is it IN the working memory, named? For particle-field techniques: the flow-field model (Amendment A5 §4: one constant flow field, borrowing with low-amplitude jitter, never-borrowed reserve fraction, release with velocity continuity) AND Owner Cure 1 (foreground/background intensity separation riding the borrow flag) AND Owner Cure 2 (strict phrase sequencing / phase exclusivity). For typography techniques: the typography construction precedent (Amendment A1 §2: runtime sampling of config-rendered text). Guidance that exists in INSTRUCTION but is absent from the wave's working memory is scored as absent.
    16	(6) CONSUMER NAMED — §1.4: which production surface lifts this machinery (container type + owning lane), named per item, not "production generally."
    17	(7) CODEX/OWNER INPUTS — were any Codex calls fired in this Observe (e.g. a record audit of a prior attempt's codex/ returns) with receipts filed, or is the absence printed? Does the wave need owner-only information (it almost never does — recreation prices from packets and filed scores); if claimed, is it routed as a named gap rather than silently assumed?
    18	Score 0–1 per dimension (§4), classify defects from the taxonomy, return one verdict per item.
    19	
    20	## 3. Context contract (masked view)
    21	- FED: RUN.md Observe gate-out blocks · ../QUEUE.md recreation-queue section (current) · each item's packet digest.md technique section + TECHNIQUES.md entry · prior scores.md + verdict-history.md lines for the item and its named family siblings · INSTRUCTION Amendments A1/A3/A5 guidance lines relevant to the item's family · any Observe-phase Codex receipts filed this cycle.
    22	- NEVER FED: the builder's confidence prose · HQ's supervision faces · scores from attempts not yet filed (unfiled scores do not exist).
    23	- Ceiling: ≤32k tokens; packet sections enter as the technique's section only, never the whole digest; evidence frames are referenced by path/timestamp, never fed as images (text-only judge).
    24	
    25	## 4. Output space
    26	- Verdict classes (per item): **ADVANCE · ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS · RETURN-TO-OBSERVE**.
    27	- Dimensions (0–1): queue-state-priced · prior-scores-read · mechanics-seen · variables-extracted · guidance-carried · consumer-named. (1.0 = evidenced in the record with citations; 0.5 = asserted without citation; 0.0 = absent.)
    28	- Rejection taxonomy (one primary per returned item): QUEUE-STALE (queue position/status not read this cycle) · REATTEMPT-MISROUTED (scored technique in a first-attempt wave) · SCORES-UNREAD (prior scores/cures exist, uncited) · MECHANICS-UNSEEN (no firsthand sub-beat record) · VARIABLES-THIN (variable list cannot bind a parameter table) · GUIDANCE-DROPPED (standing family guidance absent from working memory) · CONSUMER-VAGUE.
    29	- Accepted profiles travel: cited in RUN.md at the Plan gate; ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS items carry their gap list into §2 as named Plan charges.
    30	
    31	## 5. Floors and disposition
    32	- Any dimension < 0.5 → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE for that item. GUIDANCE-DROPPED on a particle-field or typography item → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE at any other score (T15 attempt 1's founding lesson: the frozen-flow defect and both owner catches were guidance-shaped failures discovered only after the wave was spent).
    33	- ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS requires every gap named with its Plan-phase cure; an unnamed gap is a RETURN.
    34	- Disposition: the verdict is advisory — reviewed by the runner, applied or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. The verdict + primary classification + disposition land in RUN.md either way.
    35	
    36	## Call command
    37	- Defined prompt + context assembly per §3, executed through the fleet's sealed decision-model route named in guards.md when bound. Binding the exact runner command here is the first firing's own first step. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.**
    38	
    39	## 6. Firing record and improvement
    40	- Exemplars: (a) T15 Cycle-002's Observe record reconstructed from its RUN.md (must ADVANCE — mechanics, timings and consumer were recorded before building). (b) A constructed record proposing T15 as a wave item for attempt 2 (must RETURN-TO-OBSERVE as REATTEMPT-MISROUTED). (c) A constructed particle-technique record with no flow-field / Owner Cure 1 / Owner Cure 2 lines (must RETURN as GUIDANCE-DROPPED). (d) A constructed record whose variable list names only "text and color" for a timed multi-phrase technique (must RETURN as VARIABLES-THIN).
    41	- Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; its firing record and misses are its improvement material. No test precedes firing. The exemplars above stand as its first firing cases — all four must classify correctly when fired, and a miss is recorded in Condense as improvement material, never as a bar to firing.
    42	
    43	## 7. Iteration (Condense)
    44	Amendments name forcing evidence + before/after. A text change takes effect on the call's next firing; the call keeps firing every cycle, and Condense prices the change against the returns that follow it. First expected amendment pressure: whether family-sibling scores (leg 2) should be mandatory for all items or only same-machinery families — priced from the first waves' returns.
     1	# Jev call — jev-plan-exit (recreation)
     2	
     3	_Per-call definition from jev-call-template.md. Built 2026-11-14 (phase-guard augmentation). The judgment: Execute is spent only on a Plan that already contains its checklists, its failure points, and its plateau exposure — priced in Plan, never discovered at close._
     4	
     5	## 1. What it judges
     6	- Deliverable: per-item Plan product in RUN.md (§2 gate out: parameter table + construction choice + verification plan) plus the wave manifest's per-item summaries.
     7	- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §2, at the gate out of Plan, before §3 Execute opens for an item. The verdict is advisory per item — applied, or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
     8	
     9	## 2. Instruction (the model's charge)
    10	Judge whether this Plan can be executed and verified without improvisation, item by item. Price, in order:
    11	(1) PARAMETER TABLE COMPLETE — every variable from the Observe gate-out (§1.3 list, as passed by jev-observe-exit) is a named config key with the specimen's value as default (§2.1). A variable with no key, or animation logic the Plan already describes with literals, is a Plan failure named here — not an Execute surprise.
    12	(2) CONSTRUCTION CHOICE PRICED — the HTML-native construction is chosen for the technique's mechanics (canvas particle system · CSS keyframes · SVG draw-on · DOM animation · generated imagery + overlays) with rejected alternatives named in one line each (§2.2). For particle-field items the choice must instantiate the flow-field model (Amendment A5 §4); for typography items it must start from runtime text sampling (Amendment A1 §2) or name why not. Owner Cure 1 (intensity separation) and Owner Cure 2 (phase exclusivity) appear as construction requirements where the technique is a particle field or a sequenced-phrase piece — absent cures in a particle/sequence Plan = the T15 attempt-1 failure re-planned.
    13	(3) EXECUTE CHECKLIST EXISTS — a step list for §3 (segment cut with timestamps ±0.5 s handles · recreation.html build · comparison.html build with synchronized controls + phone stacking · self-verify legs) concrete enough that a builder who did not write the Plan could execute it.
    14	(4) VERIFY CHECKLIST EXISTS, AS INSTRUMENTS — §2.4's verification plan names: the swap test's exact altered values (words minimum + one timing + one palette value, §5.1) · the purity greps + asset inventory (§5.2/§6.1) · the comparison check (§5.3) · jev-prewave's call point (§5, between own checks and the wave) · the five-lens Codex wave composition (§5.4: motion fidelity · timing/tempo · construction purity · reusability · readability). A checklist item stated as an intention ("check purity") without its instrument (the grep patterns / harness) fails this leg.
    15	(5) FAILURE POINTS EVALUATED — the Plan names what breaks it, per item: at minimum priced from this job's record — surplus-particle freeze (T15: motion 68 + reuse 64 convergent defect) · word-vs-reserve intensity collapse (owner catch 1, readability) · phrase-lifecycle overlap (owner catch 2) · fitting/wrapping limits for long words (reuse 64: fitting stops ~14 px, no multiline) · pool/density guards · the render-proof limitation (no browser binary in this seat — the comparison page is the render surface; the Plan must state how its absence is carried, as attempt 1's scores.md did). Technique-specific failure points beyond this floor are expected; a Plan whose failure list is only this floor, copied, is scored down on specificity.
    16	(6) PLATEAU FLOOR PRICED IN PLAN — the floor rule (Amendment A2, practice §floor as close-out gate) is priced HERE: the Plan states the item's prior average where one exists in its family line or states FIRST-ATTEMPT (no prior), and names in advance what a non-beating result would mean (which lens is expected to be stuck, the hypothesized cause, the WHY the scores.md entry will carry). A re-attempt-shaped build (same machinery family, e.g. T16 on T15's pool) that reaches close-out and discovers its plateau there has failed this leg retroactively — the Condense record says so.
    17	(7) REDUCTIONS NAMED — anything the Plan quietly drops from the packet's mechanics (a sub-beat deferred, a phase simplified) is named as a deferral with its reason (§2/jev-prewave fidelity-plan honesty); a silent deferral found here is classified, not absorbed.
    18	Score 0–1 per dimension (§4), classify, return one verdict per item.
    19	
    20	## 3. Context contract (masked view)
    21	- FED: RUN.md Plan gate-out blocks + wave manifest · the Observe gate-out blocks with jev-observe-exit's filed verdicts · the item's scores.md / family scores.md cure lists where they exist · INSTRUCTION §2, §5, §6 + Amendments A1/A2/A5 · guards.md command list.
    22	- NEVER FED: builder rationale prose about expected scores · prior waves' verdicts for unrelated techniques · any lens return not yet filed.
    23	- Ceiling: ≤32k tokens; recreation.html does not exist yet at this gate and is never fed.
    24	
    25	## 4. Output space
    26	- Verdict classes (per item): **EXECUTE · REVISE · RETURN-TO-OBSERVE**.
    27	- Dimensions (0–1): parameter-table-complete · construction-priced · execute-checklist-ready · verify-checklist-instrumented · failure-points-priced · plateau-priced.
    28	- Rejection taxonomy (one primary): UNBOUND-VARIABLE · LITERAL-IN-LOGIC · CURE-ABSENT (Owner Cure 1/2 or family guidance missing from construction) · CHECKLIST-INTENTION (Verify item without instrument) · FAILURE-POINTS-GENERIC · PLATEAU-UNPRICED · SILENT-DEFERRAL · RETURN-TO-OBSERVE-ROOT (the Plan's defect is an Observe defect — mechanics/variables missing upstream).
    29	- Accepted profiles travel: cited in RUN.md at the Execute gate; REVISE items carry their classified defect as the Plan amendment charge.
    30	
    31	## 5. Floors and disposition
    32	- verify-checklist-instrumented < 0.5 → REVISE (a Plan that cannot say how it will check itself does not execute). CURE-ABSENT on a particle-field or sequenced item → REVISE at any other score. PLATEAU-UNPRICED on a family re-use build → REVISE.
    33	- RETURN-TO-OBSERVE is reserved for defects whose cure is upstream (missing mechanics/variables), and names the jev-observe-exit dimension that passed it — that citation is the observe-exit's firing-record evidence.
    34	- Disposition: the verdict is advisory — reviewed by the runner, applied or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. The verdict + disposition land in RUN.md either way.
    35	
    36	## Call command
    37	- Defined prompt + context assembly per §3, executed through the fleet's sealed decision-model route named in guards.md when bound. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.**
    38	
    39	## 6. Firing record and improvement
    40	- Exemplars: (a) T15 attempt 1's Plan reconstructed from Cycle-002 RUN.md (must EXECUTE or REVISE only on named legs — it did carry a verification plan and a named interlude deferral). (b) A constructed particle Plan with no intensity-separation requirement (must REVISE as CURE-ABSENT). (c) A constructed Plan whose Verify checklist reads "run swap test, check purity, fire wave" with no altered values or grep patterns (must REVISE as CHECKLIST-INTENTION). (d) A constructed T16 Plan silent on T15's 78.5 and its stuck lenses (must REVISE as PLATEAU-UNPRICED).
    41	- Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; its firing record and misses are its improvement material. No test precedes firing. The exemplars above stand as its first firing cases — all four must classify correctly when fired, and a miss is recorded in Condense as improvement material, never as a bar to firing.
    42	
    43	## 7. Iteration (Condense)
    44	Amendments name forcing evidence + before/after. A text change takes effect on the call's next firing; the call keeps firing every cycle, and Condense prices the change against the returns that follow it. Standing watch: whether the §2.4 "four lenses" wording anywhere still survives against the five-lens form — any Plan citing four lenses is a FAILURE-POINTS-GENERIC signal, not a typo.
    45	
    46	## Amendment — allocation/count consistency leg (2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 025 Condense, pattern promotion)
    47	**The leg:** for every item whose Plan carries a schedule or allocation table, this gate prices the table's **census-anchor mapping** before Execute: each prescribed onset/duration is mapped into segment-relative time (window-start offset applied) and cross-checked against every census state the wave record names for that item. A prescribed value that contradicts a named census state at its instant (e.g. a front prescribed 8% grown at the census instant whose state reads "no territory"; arrivals prescribed complete at 11300 ms against a census anchor "crowded by ~7000 ms") is a REVISE charge, primary class **UNBOUND-SCHEDULE**. A Plan whose schedule table prints no census-anchor mapping is priced as carrying an unmapped schedule — the mapping's absence is itself the charge (the table cannot be checked, which is the defect's hiding place). Count assertions ride the same leg: a summary count in the Plan that disagrees with the table it summarizes is UNBOUND-SCHEDULE's count form (A9.3's gate side).
    48	**Forcing evidence (three instances, one class):** T153 Wave 21 (timing 45 — §2b allocation contradicted the §1c census checkpoints it claimed to rest on) · T160 Wave 22 (timing 68 — prescribed onsets 2500/3500 ms already 8.33%/45.45% grown at the 449 s/452 s census instants) · T162 Wave 22 (timing 64 — even-stepped allocation completing at 11300 ms against census anchors at ~2000/~7000 ms). For T160 and T162 the build implemented the prescribed schedule exactly (verified from this cycle's filed returns, bound in Cycle 025 RUN §9b item 2); for T153 the same compliance is attributed to the seat's Wave-21 cycle record (Cycle 024 RUN §5) and is unverified in the Wave-22 stream. In all three the defect was the Plan's, discovered by the timing lens at the cost of the item's verdict.
    49	**Before/after:** before — this gate priced parameter tables for completeness and checklists for instruments, but no leg owned schedule-vs-census consistency, so three instances across Waves 21–22 shipped census-contradicting schedules through a fired gate. After — the mapping is a named Plan product and this leg prices it at the gate, where the cure costs a table edit instead of a verdict.
     1	# Jev call — jev-prewave (recreation)
     2	
     3	_Per-call definition from jev-call-template.md. Designed 2026-11-14. The judgment: a scoring wave is the lane's expensive instrument — this call prices whether a build has EARNED its wave before the wave spends._
     4	
     5	## 1. What it judges
     6	- Deliverable: an attempt's build record (parameter table · construction route · own-checks results) BEFORE the Codex wave fires.
     7	- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §4, between the builder's own checks (§5.2) and the wave (§5.3). The verdict is advisory: applied, a HOLD returns the build to the builder with named defects and the wave does not fire on that item; set aside, the miss is recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
     8	
     9	## 2. Instruction (the model's charge)
    10	Judge whether this build record shows a recreation ready to be scored, or one whose defects are already visible in its own paperwork. Price: (1) PARAMETERIZATION — is the piece genuinely CONFIG-driven (fields named, ranges sane), or hard-coded with a config costume? (2) PURITY PRE-CHECK — does the construction route describe generation from parameters, with no tracing/embedding step hiding in the prose? (3) OWN-CHECKS COMPLETENESS — are the mechanical guards' results recorded (purity grep, swap test, syntax), or asserted? **Census-checkpoint mapping (Amendment A11, landed 2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense): every Observe census checkpoint for the item must map to an executable own-check assertion whose evaluation instant is CONFIG-derived; the build-record identifies checkpoint · assertion · CONFIG expression · evaluated result. ASSERTED-CHECKS is returned if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent; a CONFIG timing swap must be shown to move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Receipt form (Amendment A12, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense): the execution evidence for each assertion is its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT — harness command or run · CONFIG expression evaluated · raw result from the build under review (for a timing swap, the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant); a claim without its receipt is execution evidence absent. **Receipt-index ground (Amendment A13, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense): a build-record whose RECEIPT INDEX (INSTRUCTION A13.1) is missing an expected entry (an applicable guards.md command, a planned A11 assertion, an assertion inherited whole from a prior attempt's filed harness, or a census row for an expected CONFIG key), carries an exclusion whose disposition cites no governing plan or guard, or carries a populated receipt lacking the evidence its assertion requires (CONFIG expression + evaluated value for CONFIG-derived inputs; raw observed result for checks) is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground by name.** The same leg prices the A6 fit evidence: a fit-table row lacking measurement provenance, or carrying model-derived bounds, per guard-measured-fit.md checks 1–2 is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground.** (4) TECHNIQUE FIDELITY PLAN — does the record state which packet mechanics the build implements and which it deliberately defers (a deferral named is lawful; a mechanic silently absent is not)? Score 0–1 per dimension, classify defects. You judge paperwork only: a build can pass you and still fail its wave — your job is that no wave is spent on a build its own record already condemns.
    11	
    12	## 3. Context contract (masked view)
    13	- FED: build-record.md · the CONFIG block of recreation.html · the technique's packet section · guards.md command list (what own-checks should exist) · **the item's A6 leg outputs (fit-table.md + config-census.md) — added 2026-11-16, recreation Cycle 024 Condense, on the Wave-21 pattern: prewave firings for T151, T153 and T154 all HOLDed or re-fired on feed completeness (the A6 files and packet section existed complete in the artifact directory but were not in the payload), the lane's recurring ASSERTED-CHECKS false-positive class. A payload lacking any FED element is a feeder defect, printed as such in the build record; a HOLD whose only named cure is feeding an already-filed FED element is disposed as a feed-completeness miss, with the miss recorded.**
    14	- FED (added 2026-11-17, Cycle 026 Condense — the T167 miss): **the wave record's binding census-anchor mapping for the item + any Observe dispositions pricing source ambiguities** (the §1d-form: where a packet caption or digest line admits two readings, the wave record's priced reading governs). A HOLD founded on a source ambiguity the wave record has already priced is a feeder defect, disposed as such in the build record — the judge prices the build against the binding mapping, not against raw source prose. (Founding miss: Cycle 026 T167 — HOLD priced a packet caption's ambiguous reading against a build that followed the gate-approved mapping; the seat upheld the set-aside at §5.)
    15	- NEVER FED: the builder's confidence prose · prior attempts' scores (each build is priced on its own record).
    16	- Ceiling: ≤32k tokens; the HTML enters as its CONFIG + construction sections, not media.
    17	
    18	## 4. Output space
    19	- Verdict classes: **FIRE-WAVE · HOLD**.
    20	- Dimensions (0–1): parameterization · purity pre-check · own-checks completeness · fidelity-plan honesty.
    21	- Rejection taxonomy (one primary): HARDCODED-CONFIG · TRACING-STEP · ASSERTED-CHECKS (results claimed, not recorded) · SILENT-DEFERRAL.
    22	- Accepted profile travels: cited in scores.md's pre-wave line; a wave fired over a HOLD is a deviation (WAVE-OVER-HOLD).
    23	
    24	## 5. Floors and disposition
    25	- Any dimension < 0.5 → HOLD · ASSERTED-CHECKS at any score on other dimensions → HOLD (unrecorded checks are the lane's named failure class).
    26	- Disposition: the verdict is advisory — reviewed by the runner, applied or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. The verdict + classification + disposition land in the build record either way; an applied HOLD leaves the item IN PROGRESS and the wave moves to its next item (a held item never holds the wave hostage).
    27	
    28	## Call command
    29	- BINDING OWED AT FIRST FIRING — the call fires in this job's next live cycle (owner's ruling 2026-11-14: arming = firing); binding it to the fleet's decision-model runner and recording the exact command here is the first firing's own first step, and the raw response files in the run record.
    30	
    31	## 6. Firing record and improvement
    32	- Exemplars: T15 attempt 1's build record (must FIRE-WAVE: checks recorded, deferral of the interlude named in its Plan) · a constructed record claiming a swap test with no harness output (must HOLD as ASSERTED-CHECKS) · a constructed record whose CONFIG is decorative over hard-coded phrases (must HOLD as HARDCODED-CONFIG).
    33	- Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; its firing record and misses are its improvement material. No test precedes firing. The exemplars above stand as its first firing cases — all three must classify correctly when fired, and a miss is recorded in Condense as improvement material, never as a bar to firing.
    34	
    35	## 7. Iteration (Condense)
    36	Amendments name forcing evidence + before/after. A text change takes effect on the call's next firing; the call keeps firing every cycle, and Condense prices the change against the returns that follow it.
    37	
    38	## Owner's ruling addendum (2026-11-14 ~20:55 EST — supersedes gate phrasing above)
    39	ARMING = FIRING: this call fires unconditionally in its owning job's next live cycle; the raw response files in the run record. There is no BUILT-NOT-FIRED state and no calibration gate — the calibration exemplars above are improvement material the firing record tests, not a precondition. VERDICTS ARE ADVISORY: applied, or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense + the call-file amendment it teaches. Any sentence above phrasing this call as blocking, gating, or preconditioning a step reads superseded by this addendum; the FIRING is the only non-skippable part.

