    18	4. **CONFIG and construction support parameterization and purity.** Tile geometry, phase timing, label content, palette and arrow geometry flow into the SVG from CONFIG. The construction record and source-reference scan show generation from those values. Reusability has a narrower gap: `framePx` uses `enslavedPx` without consulting `camp`, and the content swap gives both North tiles zero thickness. That swap verifies the supplied values, while a South-only rule across configurations would require a validator or an explicit camp predicate and a swap that exercises it. [Recreation CONFIG and `stateAt`](recreation.html) · [Build record §2, `SWAP-CONTENT`](build-record.md)
    19	
    20	5. **The fidelity plan names its departures and follows the binding source interpretation.** Observe prices the arrows as rule announcements and keeps the tiles in their camps, with free population shown by area and enslaved population by added frames. The build record names the map, silhouettes and three-fifths tail as deferrals. Its independent arrow-phase claim is only partly supported by the renderer. The free arrow path opacity follows `freeLabelOpacity`, and the arrowhead waits for full label opacity. At C@4000 the receipt shows `arrowsP=1` and label progress about `0.222`, which proves path completion in state but leaves visible arrow completion unproved. The record could state that coupling explicitly or file a renderer-level receipt for the behaviour prescribed in the Plan. [Observe/Plan §§1.2–1.3 and 2.2](../../../study-jobs/recreation/runs/2026-11-18-cycle-039-wave-36/item-T218-observe-plan.md) · [Build record §4](build-record.md#4-fidelity-plan-implemented--deferred) · [Recreation `render`](recreation.html)
