item-T218-observe-plan.md:25:Frames extracted with ffmpeg from source.webm into the artifact dir `census/` at 2 s spacing (seg-rel ms = source − 271 s), each viewed firsthand, plus a 1 s fine set in the transition zones (extracted at the §2b cure round, viewed firsthand):
item-T218-observe-plan.md:74:## §2 — PLAN (AS AMENDED at §2b — all gate cures applied in this text)
item-T218-observe-plan.md:78:Derived (named, not stored): tile scale at t (tiny→small→free interpolation) · tile fill (tileStart→tile lerp by eased free progress) · frame thickness = enslavedPx × eased enslaved progress · freeLabelOpacity (in by label phase, out by label-out phase) · enslavedLabelOpacity (in by its phase, out by its out-phase) · arrow endpoints — resolved at derive time from the CONFIG target labels (tile of that label, else the first tile of that label's camp in the specimen camp map, else the first tile of the camp) to the target tile's current top-edge point; apex from the CONFIG apex fractions × stage · completeAtMs = tEnslavedLabelOutMs + enslavedLabelOutDurMs = 18500 · durationMs = completeAtMs + holdMs = 21000. **Phase-order invariant (validation-enforced, tightened at §2b):** all durations > 0 and finite; tFreeMs ≥ appear end; tFreeMs ≤ tArrowsMs and arrows end ≤ free end; tFreeMs ≤ tFreeLabelMs and free-label end ≤ free end; tFreeLabelOutMs ≥ free end; tEnslavedMs ≥ free-label-out end; tEnslavedLabelMs ≥ enslaved-frames end; tEnslavedLabelOutMs ≥ enslaved-label end — a violating CONFIG is rejected by validateConfig, never rendered overlapped. Negative probes: tFreeLabelMs→7000 REJECTED (label end 8500 > free end 5000) · tEnslavedMs→9000 REJECTED (before label-out end 11000). Boundary probe: tEnslavedMs = 11000 (= label-out end) ACCEPTED.
item-T218-observe-plan.md:79:Nested: `tiles[12]` — `{label, camp, cx, cy, freeW, freeH, enslavedPx}` (sizes/thicknesses are the §1.3 VISUAL ESTIMATES at the 640 px stage; positions AMENDED at §2b so no two tiles overlap at full size — geometry assertion in the harness): Virginia south 100,165 140×135 e15 · North Carolina south 240,144 118×118 e11 · South Carolina south 240,252 84×84 e8 · Delaware south 62,262 44×44 e3 · Maryland south 140,282 96×96 e8 · Georgia south 62,330 58×58 e4 · New Jersey south 232,338 84×84 e3 · New York north 428,168 124×120 e0 · Pennsylvania north 566,145 144×138 e0 · Connecticut north 380,278 88×94 e0 · Massachusetts north 562,275 132×120 e0 · New Hampshire north 462,345 66×84 e0. (Count assertion: tiles source-count 12 = built-count 12, harness-printed. Frame-collision rule: frames draw BEHIND tiles, so a frame extending under a neighbour tile is hidden there — the specimen's frames abut the same way; the harness asserts tile-vs-tile non-overlap at full size and every frame's extent inside the stage.)
item-T218-observe-plan.md:111:- Geometry collisions: tile slots amended at §2b to zero tile-vs-tile overlap at full size; the harness asserts it at default AND swap configurations, frames included in stage bounds.
item-T218-observe-plan.md:119:## §2b — Gate dispositions (all four fired BEFORE any build script — A9.2 satisfied)
item-T218-observe-plan.md:120:- **codex-observe → CONFIRMED-WITH-GAPS** (return: item-T218-codex-observe-return.md). Dispositions: (1) packet + register agree; the catalogue wording compresses two operations — APPLIED, already priced in §1.1–§1.3 (two-act reading, arrows as rule-announcement device). (2) The window includes adjacent scenes (map lead-in, T219 tail) — APPLIED: t=0 allocation + departure table (§2.3) + named deferrals (§2.2). (3) G3/G4 do not attach to T17 — noted, concurs with §1.1. (4) Sibling audits (T210 PASS bound to five returns, arithmetic 426/5 = 85.2 · T212 NO VERDICT bound to two HOLD returns) — APPLIED as the §1.5 sibling-cure carry. (5) Segment ffprobe binding — APPLIED as an Execute charge (§2.4 step 1 files it; it cannot exist before the cut). Note on firing order: the first firing attempt of this call (and of jev-observe-exit) was killed by a platform service restart at 0-byte returns; both were re-fired in full and the filed returns are the re-firings' — the restart is recorded here, not hidden.
item-T218-observe-plan.md:121:- **jev-observe-exit → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE, primary MECHANICS-UNSEEN** (return: item-T218-jev-observe-exit-return.md; dims: queue 1.0 · prior-scores 0.5 · mechanics 0.5 · variables 1.0 · guidance 1.0 · consumer 1.0). Dispositions: (1) continuous-motion cure — APPLIED IN THE FINE-CENSUS FORM: a 1 s fine set in every transition zone (fine-9000/11000/17000/21000/23000/27000, viewed firsthand, hashes in §1.3) tightened every transition bound (growth 280–282 s · label-out 287–288 s · frames 291–292 s · enslaved label-out 295–298 s) and the schedule in §2.1 was re-derived from those bounds; full continuous playback is SET ASIDE with reason — this seat has no player, and a ≤1 s frame census in the transitions + 2 s elsewhere prices every state change the technique contains (T212 precedent: the same set-aside stood). (2) Prior-score cure — APPLIED: §1.5 now cites T210's and T212's filed cures by name and binds them to §2.3/§2.4. (3) RUN.md §1's "tile move" summary wording — NOTED for the seat (RUN.md is the seat's file; this item's census reading — no tile changes camp — governs the build and is filed here). The item ADVANCES on the cured record (verdicts advisory, 2026-11-14 ruling).
item-T218-observe-plan.md:122:- **codex-plan-review → REVISE** (return: item-T218-codex-plan-review-return.md). Dispositions: (1) Convergent freeze inapplicable by construction — noted; its transferable lesson APPLIED (P6/P7 print full predicates: every tile's scale + frame). (2) Tile-slot overlaps (NC/SC 6 px · PA/MA 23 px) — APPLIED: slots re-derived in §2.1 to zero tile-vs-tile overlap, harness geometry assertion at default + swap. (3) Validator sequencing hole (label could end after growth) — APPLIED: tightened invariant in §2.1 + negative probes (late label, early enslaved) + boundary probe in §2.4. (4) Presentation bindings (wrap limits, line spacing, halo, label-out easing) — APPLIED: labelLineHeight/labelHaloPx bound in §2.1; easings are per-phase CONFIG keys. (5) Comparison clamp derived from durationMs — APPLIED (§2.4 step 3: the comparison derives durationMs from recreation.html's CONFIG at runtime). (6) Arrow endpoints bound to target tiles — APPLIED: freeArrowTargets/enslavedArrowTarget + apex fractions in §2.1, endpoints resolved at derive time (the draft's raw normalized paths placed the apex at x=512 against a label centred at 320 — cured). (7) Fixed source-alignment probe beside each CONFIG-relative probe + raw/eased printed separately + full predicates — APPLIED in §2.3 (C* probes + receipt form). (8) Build-zero rename + CP3 opacity departure — APPLIED (Z0, §2.3). (9) Motion predicted minimum + readability floor risk — APPLIED in §2.5. (10) The review's CANNOT-READ note on build-record.md — expected at Plan stage (no build exists yet); no disposition needed.
item-T218-observe-plan.md:123:- **jev-plan-exit → REVISE, primary UNBOUND-SCHEDULE** (return: item-T218-jev-plan-exit-return.md; dims: parameter 0.75 · construction 0.90 · execute 0.80 · verify 0.65 · failure 0.75 · plateau 1.00). Dispositions: census-anchor table — APPLIED point by point in the amended §2.1 schedule + §2.3 (arrows on their own phase with C@4000 asserting arrows complete while the label is partial · label/arrows asserted at C@6000/C@10000 · bare state at C@12000 · enslaved label/arrow + per-tile frames at C@16000/C@20000 · CP3 mid-fade Z0 form · lead-in/tail departures printed). Swap centres specified (§2.4) · sync formula explicit (§2.4) · exact comparison labels (§2.4) · five lenses spelled out (§2.4) · geometry check (§2.5) · PIL ink measurement replacing the nominal-size claim (§2.4/§2.5). The return's Limits note (observe-exit return empty at its firing) is cured by the re-fired return now on file.
