item-T227-observe-plan.md:60:`stageW 640 · stageH 400 · objCX 300 · objCY 205 · objW 190 · objH 230 · objTiltDeg -78 (saw-phase tilt; present phase 0) · segCols 4 · segRows 5 · segGroovePx 5 · headPresent true · headH 52 · bladeLen 300 · bladeW 64 · bladeAngleDeg -90 (edge vertical at contact, rotating with tilt) · bladeTravelPx 150 · sawSteps 5 · strokeAmpPx 14 · handW 150 · handH 110 · handHolder {x 205, y 300} · handGuide {x 430, y 120} · plankCount 5 · skinRimPx 6 · fleshMaxWPx 46 · tPresentMs 0 · presentDurMs 900 · tSawMs 900 · sawDurMs 2600 · fleshOnsetFrac 0.62 · partGapMs 0 · partDurMs 700 · seamWPx 7 · holdMs 800 · easeSaw "stepped" · easePart "easeInOut" · palette {board #8a5a33, plank #6e4525, shell #44543c, shellLight #5c7050, shellDark #2e3a28, head #6b6f66, lever #7d8178, pin #8f938a, blade #b9bcbe, bladeEdge #e8eaea, hand #d9a184, flesh #7ec850, fleshLight #a8e063, skin #3d5a2a} · outer {name "grenade", shellKey "shell"} · inner {name "avocado", fleshKey "flesh"}` — identities are CONFIG DATA: `outer`/`inner` carry the names + which palette roles they bind; the swap test replaces the pair wholesale INCLUDING the shellKey/fleshKey fields (see §2.4). Hand phase-presence is DERIVED, not stored: holder present in every phase; guide present during present+saw, withdrawn during part (its withdrawal is part of the part phase). (Table AS AMENDED at §2b.)
