item-T232-observe-plan.md:65:Top-level (AS AMENDED at §2b — knife/saw/product bindings added, slicing retimed to census, chop lead 500): `stageW 640 · stageH 400 · boardX 40 · boardY 96 · boardW 560 · boardH 264 · boardRadiusPx 26 · domeCx 320 · domeCy 300 · domeR 92 · stripCount 3 · stripGapPx 10 · sliceDurMs 1000 · sawAmpPx 7 · sawCycles 3 · knifeRestX 96 · knifeRestY 64 · knifeBladeLenPx 300 · knifeBladeHPx 64 · knifeHandleLenPx 74 · knifeHandleHPx 20 · knifeAngleDeg -4 · chopLeadMs 500 · chopTravelPx 118 · settleFrac 0.12 · settleDurMs 400 · holdMs 500 · seed 23209 · productKind "dice" · pipStyle "dots" · stackLayerDyFrac 0.62 · easeSaw "easeInOut" · easeChop "easeIn" · easeSettle "easeInOut"` — AMENDED at the prewave cure round: the draft's `fontFamily` key is REMOVED (the recreation carries no text, and the comparison page's font stack is its own CSS — no CONFIG key may claim a binding it does not drive). The strip-hold interval is DERIVED, not a key: hold runs [sliceDurMs, passes[0].tMs − chopLeadMs] = [1000, 2000] — the earlier draft's `tHoldStripsMs` key is removed (jev-plan-exit gap 3: the key had no defined application).
